+inside `msgstr` also work. **ICU `date` / `time` in a `msgstr` are now measured, and on this PO setup a
+*styleless* one is wrong — prefer the format module for dates and times.** The PO plugin imports both ICU
+`{d, date}` and `{d, time}` as the inlang `datetime` annotation, carrying a style argument through and
+passing no options when there is none; `@inlang/paraglide-js@2.27.0` then fills an option-less `datetime`
+with its default `dateStyle=medium timeStyle=short`, which `2.26.0` and below dropped. So on `^2` today,
+`Due {d, date}` renders `Due Jan 15, 2026, 2:30 PM` — a time nobody asked for — where the same catalog on
+`2.26.0` rendered `Due 1/15/2026`, and `At {d, time}` renders a full date on both. Neither version warns.
+A style is unaffected: `{d, date, short}` is `1/15/26` on both. If a catalog must carry an ICU date or
+time, **always give it a style**; on the ICU-JSON format (`json-format.convert.md`) the `plugin-icu1`
+import keeps ICU's own defaults and a styleless `{d, date}` is correct from `2.27.0` on.)
 
